lesson: 93
title: The change from a payment
stars: 0
explain: A dollar is 100 cents. The change is what you paid minus what the things cost.
explain: 3 cookies at 25 cents cost 75 cents; paying with 1 dollar (100 cents) gives 100 − 75 = 25 cents of change.
vars: a=name i=item n=2..5 p5=1..19 d=1..5
let: p = p5 * 5
let: pay = d * 100
need: n * p < pay
answer: pay - n * p
exercise: {a} buys {n} {i}s at {p} cents each and pays with {d} dollars. How many cents of change does {a.he} get?
exercise: One {i} costs {p} cents. {a} buys {n} {i}s and gives the seller {d} dollars. How much change, in cents, does {a.he} get back?
exercise: {a} has {d} dollars. {a.He} buys {n} {i}s for {p} cents each. How many cents does {a.he} get in change?
exercise: {n} {i}s cost {p} cents each. {a} pays with {d} dollars. What is the change in cents?
exercise: {a} pays {d} dollars for {n} {i}s that cost {p} cents apiece. How many cents should the seller give back?
test: The seller takes {d} dollars from {a} for {n} {i}s, each priced at {p} cents. How many cents does the seller return?
test: How many cents come back to {a} if {a.he} hands over {d} dollars for {n} {i}s at {p} cents a piece?
test: With {d} dollars in {a.his} hand, {a} buys {n} {i}s. Every {i} is {p} cents. How many cents are left over after paying?
test: {a} gives {d} dollars at the counter. {a.His} {n} {i}s cost {p} cents each. What change does {a.he} receive, in cents?
exercise: {a} pays {d} dollars for {n} {i}s. Each {i} is {p} cents. How many cents of change are there?
exercise: How many cents of change does {a} get after buying {n} {i}s at {p} cents apiece with {d} dollars?
exercise: {n} {i}s, {p} cents each, paid with {d} dollars. How many cents come back?
exercise: At a store in Vermont, {a} gives the cashier {d} dollars for {n} {i}s that cost {p} cents per {i}. How many cents of change does {a.he} get?
exercise: {a} has {d.words} dollars and buys {n.words} {i}s at {p} cents each. How many cents does {a.he} still have?
exercise: Every {i} costs {p} cents. {a} takes {n} of them and pays with {d} dollars. What change, in cents, is {a.he} given?
exercise: {a} spends money on {n} {i}s at {p} cents each from the {d} dollars {a.he} has. How many cents remain?
exercise: A shop in Ottawa sells {i}s for {p} cents each. {a} buys {n} and pays {d} dollars. How much change does {a.he} get, in cents?
test: How much change in cents is due when {d} dollars pay for {n} {i}s priced {p} cents each?
test: {a} goes to a school fair in Ontario with {d} dollars. {a.He} spends {p} cents on each of {n} {i}s. How many cents are still in {a.his} pocket?
test: The cashier gets {d} dollars from {a}. The {n} {i}s are {p} cents per {i}. How many cents does the cashier hand back?
test: After {a} pays for {n} {i}s at {p} cents each, how many cents are left of {a.his} {d} dollars?
test: {a} hands {d} dollars across the counter for {n.words} {i}s, every one costing {p} cents. How much change comes back, in cents?
test: {p} cents each, {n} {i}s, a payment of {d} dollars: how many cents of change?
exercise: {a} buys {n} {i}s, {p}c each, pays {d} dollar. change in cents?
exercise: {n+1} {i}s no wait {n} {i}s, {p} cents each, handed over {d} dollars. how much change back in cents
exercise: {a} reckons the change is {pay+n*p} cents cos {a.he} added it. nah. {n} {i}s at {p}c, paid {d} dollars, whats the change in cents
exercise: got {d} dollars, getting {n} {i}s at {p} cents — my bus is in 10 min — how much change in cents
test: paid {d} dollars for {n} {i}s, {p}c a pop. whats back in cents
test: {i}s are {p} cents each, {a} gets {n} and gives {d+1} dollars, no sorry, {d} dollars. change in cents?
test: {a} said change is {pay-p} cents cos {a.he} only counted one {i}. {n} {i}s at {p}c, {d} dollars paid. real change in cents?
exam: It is given that {a} purchases {n} {i}s at {p} cents each and tenders {d} dollars in payment. Determine the change due, in cents.
exam: Ascertain the sum in cents to be returned to a purchaser who, having acquired {n.words} {i}s priced at {p} cents apiece, remits {d.words} dollars.
exam: Whereas the price of one {i} is {p} cents and {a} pays {d} dollars for {n} {i}s, compute the change, in cents, to which {a.he} is entitled.
exam: State the amount of change, expressed in cents, which is owed to {a} pursuant to a payment of {d} dollars for {n} {i}s at {p} cents per {i}.
exercise: Money's a bit tight, so {a} takes only {d} dollars to the shop and buys {n} {i}s at {p} cents each. How many cents of change does {a.he} bring home?
exercise: Dad is "between jobs", so he gives {a} exactly {d} dollars for the shopping. {a} buys {n} {i}s at {p} cents each. How many cents does {a.he} hand back to Dad?
test: {n} {i}s at {p}c each, i paid {d} dollars. how much change. and if they've slapped a "convenience fee" on it there's gonna be trouble
